From: Fabric Production Readiness Agent <agent@fabric.dev>
Date: 2026-01-15
Subject: [PATCH 005] Frontend Test Coverage Thresholds (P0)

Problem:
- Coverage thresholds in vite.config.ts and vitest.config.ts exclude
  virtually all application source code (components, pages, hooks, routes,
  shell, governance, contexts are all excluded).
- The 70/60/70/70 thresholds apply to ~5% of the codebase, making them
  meaningless for production readiness.
- reportOnFailure is not set, so CI does not fail when thresholds are missed.

Solution:
1. Remove overly broad exclusions so coverage applies to the actual
   application source code.
2. Keep only legitimate exclusions: generated API code, test files,
   entry points, config files, and type definitions.
3. Add reportOnFailure: true so CI gates enforce thresholds.
4. Add a CI workflow step that fails the build when coverage drops
   below the enterprise thresholds.

Targets: 70% lines, 60% branches, 65% functions, 65% statements.

